As another example of stack application, consider adding very large num- 
bers. The largest magnitude of integers is limited, so we are not able to add 
18,274,364,583,929,273,748,459,595,684,373 and 8,129,498,165,026,350,236, because 
integer variables cannot hold such large values, let alone their sum. The problem can 
be solved if we treat these numbers as strings of numerals, store the numbers cor-
responding to these numerals on two stacks, and then perform addition by popping 
numbers from the stacks. The pseudocode for this algorithm is as follows:
